From 4043bf283d5da6ac0fb3ef41ce3110680cf3f3b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bvn13 <from.github@bvn13.me>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 21:53:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(plugins): let plugins contribute a section to the
 sidebar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The main area already has a generic mechanism for plugin tabs; the sidebar has
none, so a plugin whose content belongs next to the project list has nowhere to
go.

A manifest may now carry an optional sidebar object — label, icon, order,
replacesTab — validated and normalised on the server, so only known fields
reach the client. Its chip joins the built-in ones in a single ordered row
(projects 100, conversations 200, running 300, archived 400), which lets a
plugin place itself anywhere in that row by data alone. While a plugin section
is active the search box is hidden, and replacesTab keeps the plugin from
appearing both in the sidebar and in the main-area tabs.

slot stays 'tab' on purpose: adding a new slot value would fail validation on
every older host, so such a plugin could not be installed at all.

With no sidebar-declaring plugin enabled, the sidebar behaves exactly as
before.
